= Supplementary material: Reproducibility & Preregistration Audit Table <sec:audit>

This audit preserves the repository locations displaced from the main narrative. All paths are relative to the repository root. Audit numbers link the physical tests to their records; they are not additional scientific results.

Legacy audit baseline (rows 1--43): #text("71ffb99863​465b7dbc8f​7912571af9​c32626f339 (2026-10-15T22:41:51+13:00)"), including then-uncommitted manuscript and research edits. The October follow-up rows 44--48 pin evidence at revision 0de4d38. In legacy rows the Git field gives the earliest commit located for that path at audit time (hash and committer timestamp), not proof that the hypothesis was committed before measurement. Document dates are author-recorded dates; migration commits can be later. Missing seeds or registration evidence must not be inferred from these timestamps.

The source and recipe locations below retain commands, full seed schedules, windows, input hashes and exclusions where recorded. Seed excerpts are quoted literally from those sources; they may describe sampling or bootstrap seeds rather than walker seeds. Blank-board deterministic runs need no random seed. “Not located” means this audit did not recover an explicit seed declaration, not that a run was unseeded.

